      "text": "To find the sum of the geometric series \\(1 + 2 + 4 + 8 + 16 + \\cdots + 1024\\), we first need to determine the number of terms in the series. The general form of a geometric series is given by:\n\n\\[a + ar + ar^2 + ar^3 + \\cdots + ar^n\\]\n\nwhere \\(a\\) is the first term, \\(r\\) is the common ratio, and \\(n\\) is the number of terms. In this series, the first term \\(a\\) is 1, the common ratio \\(r\\) is 2, and the last term is 1024. We can find the number of terms \\(n\\) by solving for \\(n\\) in the equation:\n\n\\[ar^n = 1024\\]\n\\[1 \\cdot 2^n = 1024\\]\n\\[2^n = 1024\\]\n\nWe know that \\(1024 = 2^{10}\\), so:\n\n\\[2^n = 2^{10}\\]\n\\[n = 10\\]\n\nSo, the number of terms in the series is 10. The sum \\(S_n\\) of the first \\(n\\) terms of a geometric series is given by:\n\n\\[S_n = a \\frac{r^n - 1}{r - 1}\\]\n\nSubstituting the values \\(a = 1\\), \\(r = 2\\), and \\(n = 10\\) into the formula, we get:\n\n\\[S_{10} = 1 \\frac{2^{10} - 1}{2 - 1} = 2^{10} - 1\\]\n\nWe know that \\(2^{10} = 1024\\), so:\n\n\\[S_{10} = 1024 - 1 = 1023\\]\n\nTherefore, the sum of the series \\(1 + 2 + 4 + 8 + 16 + \\cdots + 1024\\) is \\(\\boxed{1023}\\).",
