      "text": "This is a geometric series with first term \\( a = 1 \\) and common ratio \\( r = 2 \\). We need to find the sum of the series up to the term \\( 1024 \\).\n\nThe sum \\( S_n \\) of the first \\( n \\) terms of a geometric series is given by the formula:\n\\[\nS_n = a \\frac{r^n - 1}{r - 1}\n\\]\nHere, the first term \\( a = 1 \\), the common ratio \\( r = 2 \\), and we need to find the number of terms \\( n \\).\n\nWe know the last term of the series is \\( 1024 \\). The \\( n \\)-th term of a geometric series is given by:\n\\[\na r^{n-1} = 1024\n\\]\nSubstitute \\( a = 1 \\) and \\( r = 2 \\):\n\\[\n2^{n-1} = 1024\n\\]\nWe recognize that \\( 1024 = 2^{10} \\):\n\\[\n2^{n-1} = 2^{10}\n\\]\nSince the bases are the same, we can equate the exponents:\n\\[\nn-1 = 10 \\implies n = 11\n\\]\nSo, there are 11 terms in the series.\n\nNow, substitute \\( n = 11 \\), \\( a = 1 \\), and \\( r = 2 \\) into the sum formula:\n\\[\nS_{11} = 1 \\cdot \\frac{2^{11} - 1}{2 - 1} = 2^{11} - 1\n\\]\nCalculate \\( 2^{11} \\):\n\\[\n2^{11} = 2048\n\\]\nThus,\n\\[\nS_{11} = 2048 - 1 = 2047\n\\]\nTherefore, the sum of the series is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{2047}\n\\]",
